|~ `::each`, the kind of a map in a shape whose values share one shape,
   and the laws declared under it.
   The decisions it exists for: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:each
  |~~ An each stands in the shape of a value for a map a reader's data
      keys by ids, dates or names, over its first key and the shape of its
      values, the one key standing for all of them:
      `{:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape` answers
      `::shape::each{:"17" {:id ::number}}`. The key shown tells how the
      keys of the data read, and a path of the data through that key
      reads the shape, `/17/id` answering `::number`; another key of the
      data reads by the one shown, and `keys` reads them all. A map folds
      so where every key is data, an id of digits, a date or a time, a
      uuid, an address, whatever its values hold, the kinds where they
      part among them, `::each{:"0" #[::number ::string]}`; and where it
      holds more than eight names whose values, maps, vectors, sets,
      values under a tag or null, share one shape, the users of a reader's
      data. A map of names over atoms keeps them however many, the fields
      a reader reads by `get`, a key that reads as no name, `@type`, among
      them: `{:x 1 :y 2} | shape` answers `::shape{:x ::number :y ::number}`,
      as a map of fewer names or of names whose values part does. Records merge in a
      fold as they merge in a vector, a null among the values marks the
      fold `::nullable` and an empty map among the folds of a vector marks
      it `::absent`; a vector of such maps is `[::each{…}]`, a map of
      vectors `::each[…]`.
      ::link~(::shape | doc) ::link~(::any/shape | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | proves :foldsAMapKeyedByData
        |~~ A map keyed by data folds over its first key. ~~|
        ~({:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:"17" {:id ::number}})
    | proves :foldsAtomsKeyedByData
        |~~ A map keyed by data folds over atoms as well. ~~|
        ~({:"2024-01-01" 3 :"2024-01-02" 5} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:"2024-01-01" ::number})
    | proves :readsThePathThroughTheKeyItShows
        |~~ A path of the data through the key shown reads the shape. ~~|
        ~({:"17" {:id 1} :"42" {:id 2}} | shape | get /17/id | eq ::number)
    | proves :keepsAFewNamesAsARecord
        |~~ A map of a few names keeps them, the fields `get` reads. ~~|
        ~({:db {:host "h"} :cache {:host "c"}} | shape | eq ::shape{:db {:host ::string} :cache {:host ::string}})
    | proves :foldsManyNamesOfOneShape
        |~~ A map of more than eight names of one shape folds. ~~|
        ~({:a {:n 1} :b {:n 2} :c {:n 3} :d {:n 4} :e {:n 5} :f {:n 6} :g {:n 7} :h {:n 8} :i {:n 9}} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:a {:n ::number}})
    | proves :keepsTheFieldsOfAMapOfAtoms
        |~~ A map of names over atoms keeps its keys. ~~|
        ~({:x 1 :y 2} | shape | eq ::shape{:x ::number :y ::number})
    | proves :keepsManyNamesWhoseValuesPart
        |~~ A map of many names whose values part keeps its keys. ~~|
        ~({:a 1 :b "x" :c 3 :d 4 :e 5 :f 6 :g 7 :h 8 :i 9} | shape | get /b | eq ::string)
    | proves :foldsDataKeysWhoseValuesPart
        |~~ A map keyed by data folds whatever its values hold. ~~|
        ~({:"1" {:id 1} :"2" [1]} | shape | eq ::shape::each{:"1" #[{:id ::number} [::number]]})
    | proves :keepsManyFieldsOverAtoms
        |~~ A map of names over atoms keeps them however many. ~~|
        ~({:a 1 :b 2 :c 3 :d 4 :e 5 :f 6 :g 7 :h 8 :i 9} | shape | keys | count | eq 9)
    | proves :keepsAKeyThatReadsAsNoNameAmongFields
        |~~ A key that reads as no name stays a field among names. ~~|
        ~({:"@type" "Person" :name "Ann"} | shape | eq ::shape{:"@type" ::string :name ::string})
    | proves :keepsTheKeyOfAMapOfOne
        |~~ A map of one name keeps it. ~~|
        ~({:users [1]} | shape | eq ::shape{:users [::number]})
